WEBVTT

01:29.980 --> 01:35.110
<b>Fenrys the Lupine Warrior</b>

01:31.710 --> 01:35.480
<i>I don't wanna die before I even 
get to do anything! No way!</i>

01:35.480 --> 01:36.240
<i>So...</i>

01:36.570 --> 01:39.530
I'll try every magic spell I have!

01:41.720 --> 01:42.580
Don't take me for a fool!

01:44.940 --> 01:46.500
Meteoric Leap!

01:52.580 --> 01:53.630
<i>Oh, wow..</i>

01:54.920 --> 01:56.130
Earthen Rampart!

01:58.220 --> 01:59.300
Why, you—

01:59.300 --> 02:00.430
Whirlwind!

02:02.410 --> 02:04.060
Nearby Relocation!

02:06.060 --> 02:07.310
Just die!

02:08.110 --> 02:09.020
Gravitation!

02:13.550 --> 02:15.270
Wh-What is this?

02:15.270 --> 02:18.660
<i>I-I can't move... How is this possible?</i>

02:19.200 --> 02:21.650
I have to restrain her right now!

02:21.650 --> 02:23.030
Is there any magic I can use?

02:23.030 --> 02:25.470
<i>Subjugation magic is recommended.</i>

02:26.500 --> 02:27.450
Subjugation?

02:27.450 --> 02:31.330
<i>It enslaves the target, allowing you 
to control their thoughts and actions.</i>

02:32.020 --> 02:34.550
I can't do that. What else is there?

02:34.940 --> 02:36.870
Gravity Reduction!

02:36.870 --> 02:38.910
<i>The target has used magic.</i>

02:39.460 --> 02:41.140
<i>Effects negated.</i>

02:41.480 --> 02:43.590
<i>Subjugation magic is recommended.</i>

02:43.590 --> 02:44.470
I won't use that!

02:44.930 --> 02:46.460
Nearby Relocation!

02:47.170 --> 02:49.090
<i>The target has used magic.</i>

02:49.560 --> 02:51.770
<i>Effects negated.</i>

02:51.770 --> 02:54.200
<i>Subjugation magic is recommended.</i>

02:54.650 --> 02:55.520
Not happening!

02:55.520 --> 02:57.350
Meteoric Leap...

03:04.280 --> 03:06.480
<i>The target has used magic.</i>

03:06.980 --> 03:09.000
<i>Effects negated.</i>

03:09.000 --> 03:11.300
<i>Subjugation magic is recommended.</i>

03:11.300 --> 03:13.250
No! I'm not using that!

03:13.800 --> 03:16.310
I just came to a new world!

03:16.310 --> 03:17.840
I'm not bringing that shit here!

03:18.940 --> 03:20.620
My... magic...

03:25.240 --> 03:26.590
I surrender.

03:27.670 --> 03:30.710
I lack the magic to fight back any longer.

03:31.380 --> 03:34.810
There is no path in life for 
a warrior who cannot fight.

03:34.810 --> 03:37.570
Now, kill me.

03:40.470 --> 03:42.490
I don't want to kill you.

03:42.490 --> 03:45.530
I don't really like fighting to begin with.

03:47.950 --> 03:48.990
What?!

03:48.990 --> 03:52.030
I-I am a demon!

03:52.030 --> 03:55.910
A warrior of the demons who 
do battle with you humans!

03:55.910 --> 03:58.590
And you say you will let me live?

04:00.040 --> 04:04.950
Honestly, I don't care who's 
a human or who's a demon.

04:05.560 --> 04:08.600
I just don't want to kill 
someone who's surrendered.

04:08.600 --> 04:09.560
That's all.

04:15.210 --> 04:16.400
You are naïve.

04:24.990 --> 04:27.410
H-How did you take that form?!

04:27.410 --> 04:29.490
I merely undid my beast transformation...

04:33.880 --> 04:38.690
I-If you'll promise not to 
fight with humans anymore,

04:38.690 --> 04:41.550
I'm willing to let you just leave.

04:42.430 --> 04:44.500
Just not dressed like that.

04:44.500 --> 04:45.130
Oh, yeah!

04:45.440 --> 04:48.210
I should have clothes in my Bottomless Bag.

04:51.380 --> 04:52.660
Fenrys?!

04:52.660 --> 04:55.870
<i>Target has entered a sleep 
state due to magic depletion.</i>

04:56.470 --> 04:57.440
Oh, good.

04:58.420 --> 05:00.030
It's nothing serious, then.

05:05.200 --> 05:06.070
Huh...

05:06.660 --> 05:08.700
Guess there are lots of 
different types of magic.

05:11.410 --> 05:14.260
Teleportation magic? That kid?

05:14.260 --> 05:16.960
He's obviously lying. 
No way he can use that.

05:17.970 --> 05:21.200
<i>Why do I have such powerful magic?</i>

05:32.470 --> 05:36.630
<i>I'm resistant to magic, 
and I still couldn't do anything.</i>

05:38.890 --> 05:42.460
<i>I thought the humans were a fragile race...</i>

05:45.080 --> 05:47.630
My magic has fully recovered?

05:51.350 --> 05:52.370
Fenrys!

05:52.830 --> 05:54.370
Are you feeling okay?

05:54.370 --> 05:59.240
Yes. You used healing magic on 
me while I slept, didn't you?

05:59.240 --> 06:01.380
Yeah. Looks like it worked.

06:02.480 --> 06:06.840
Anyone else would have 
killed and skinned me.

06:07.490 --> 06:12.300
I, Fenrys, hereby swear to 
never fight with humans again.

06:13.260 --> 06:14.640
Fenrys...

06:15.140 --> 06:16.230
And...

06:16.230 --> 06:18.810
Because you possess such immense power,

06:18.810 --> 06:20.590
I identify you as my master.

06:20.590 --> 06:23.940
I will dedicate my life to 
repaying my debt to you.

06:23.940 --> 06:26.600
Huh? H-Hang on!

06:26.600 --> 06:28.710
You really don't need to go that far...

06:28.710 --> 06:29.630
Master...

06:29.630 --> 06:31.370
Whoa, whoa! Don't call me—

06:31.370 --> 06:34.450
I will carry your things, 
be your slave, whatever you want.

06:34.450 --> 06:36.870
Just, please, let me stay 
by your side, Master!

06:36.870 --> 06:39.770
You don't need to carry 
my things or be my slave!

06:39.770 --> 06:42.580
I have no desire to own people like that!

06:46.550 --> 06:49.230
M-Making that noise won't change my mind!

06:49.230 --> 06:51.260
I-I said no, and no means no!

06:51.930 --> 06:53.500
If I cannot be with you...

06:54.100 --> 06:55.430
all I can do is die.

06:55.430 --> 06:59.030
O-Okay, I get it! You can follow me!

06:59.030 --> 07:01.170
Just don't do this, please!

07:04.120 --> 07:05.090
Okay!

07:08.460 --> 07:11.420
The truth is... I'm not from this world.

07:11.420 --> 07:13.470
I came from a different world.

07:13.470 --> 07:14.950
A different world?

07:15.230 --> 07:17.760
I was summoned as a hero candidate,

07:17.760 --> 07:19.530
but I had no skills at all,

07:19.530 --> 07:22.190
and they can't send me back to my own world,

07:22.190 --> 07:24.920
so I was tossed out here.

07:25.300 --> 07:26.720
Shapeshift.

07:29.040 --> 07:29.880
Master?!

07:30.420 --> 07:32.850
This is what I really look like.

07:32.850 --> 07:36.720
I changed my form because people 
from the castle might be after me.

07:37.790 --> 07:41.910
I don't know what I should do 
next, or even where to go.

07:43.450 --> 07:47.320
So if you follow me, it's only 
going to make life rough for you.

07:48.370 --> 07:50.100
You'll regret it for sure.

07:53.000 --> 07:54.220
I don't mind.

07:55.980 --> 07:57.750
We lupines live solely

07:57.750 --> 08:01.750
for the one we recognize as 
our master. That's our rule.

08:02.120 --> 08:04.700
No matter who you are or where you're from,

08:04.700 --> 08:06.500
I swear to be loyal to you

08:07.040 --> 08:09.590
and live with you for the rest of my life.

08:10.470 --> 08:11.800
So...

08:12.780 --> 08:16.680
Please let me stay by your side, Master!

08:17.810 --> 08:19.160
You're really sure?

08:19.160 --> 08:20.090
Yes!

08:21.310 --> 08:22.330
Master...

08:21.310 --> 08:22.330
H-Hey!

08:22.330 --> 08:24.310
S-Stop that!

08:26.910 --> 08:30.480
What in the world happened, Hero?

08:30.480 --> 08:33.840
We sent our forces to strike the Dark Army,

08:33.840 --> 08:35.700
and you let them be destroyed?

08:35.700 --> 08:39.890
If you would allow me to say 
something about that...

08:39.890 --> 08:44.290
What was the deal with the soldiers 
you sent on this mission?

08:44.740 --> 08:49.420
They panicked and broke formation at 
the sight of a simple magic beast,

08:49.420 --> 08:54.090
and before I knew it, 
they had already been wiped out!

08:54.090 --> 08:59.300
I did everything in my power to 
save as many of them as I could!

08:59.780 --> 09:03.700
You're saying all blame lies 
with the soldiers, Hero?

09:03.700 --> 09:04.700
That's right!

09:04.700 --> 09:09.150
You should be grateful I brought 
back as many as I did! Hmph!

09:11.100 --> 09:13.570
How did the hero fare on the battlefield?

09:13.570 --> 09:14.110
Sire.

09:14.790 --> 09:18.080
Despite being the hero, 
he remained at our army's rear,

09:18.080 --> 09:20.890
he fled while the rest of 
us fought for our lives,

09:20.890 --> 09:27.330
and he yelled at others while pinning 
all responsibility on them.

09:27.330 --> 09:31.390
Several of our men have begun to 
express their displeasure with him.

09:32.720 --> 09:35.630
<i>Just what is the meaning of this?</i>

09:35.980 --> 09:38.850
<i>I've been training for the past month!</i>

09:38.850 --> 09:41.970
<i>Why haven't any of my 
skills improved at all?!</i>

09:42.380 --> 09:46.380
<i>As it stands, I could hold my own 
against humans or weak magic beasts,</i>

09:42.720 --> 09:52.190
m 0 0 l 140 0 l 140 190 l 0 190

09:42.720 --> 09:52.190
<u><b>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hLv. 91\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h 
</b></u>Strength ... 999 
Defense ... 999 
Speed ... 999 
Magic ... 999 
HP ... 999 
Skills ... 
Not yet acquired

09:46.380 --> 09:52.190
<i>but I wouldn't stand a chance against 
beasts with any degree of strength!</i>

09:53.390 --> 09:54.500
Hero!

09:54.500 --> 09:57.530
Oh, Tsuya. Sorry to keep you waiting.

09:57.530 --> 09:59.500
Not at all.

09:59.500 --> 10:04.410
Waiting for you is an important 
part of my duties as your servant.

10:05.130 --> 10:08.160
Hmph. Perfect timing. Come with me.

10:08.160 --> 10:10.630
I'll indulge you in every luxury 
with the castle's money.

10:12.110 --> 10:13.430
Okay!

10:17.770 --> 10:20.760
I'll need to earn money if I 
want to get by in this world.

10:21.220 --> 10:24.410
I think I'll go to the adventurers' 
guild to find some work,

10:24.410 --> 10:26.730
then find a place to spend the night.

10:26.730 --> 10:30.300
Understood. I will accompany you, Master.

10:30.300 --> 10:34.860
It still bothers me to hear 
you call me "Master."

10:34.860 --> 10:37.050
You could just use my name...

10:37.050 --> 10:38.570
Hey there, missus!

10:38.860 --> 10:42.660
Care for a veggie or two? 
They're fresh-picked!

10:43.160 --> 10:44.410
Missus?

10:44.410 --> 10:46.620
I guess he thought we were married.

10:46.940 --> 10:50.000
Actually, having people think 
we're a married couple

10:50.000 --> 10:53.210
might make it easier to travel 
together without looking suspicious.

10:53.600 --> 10:56.270
I mean, if it's okay with you, of course...

10:56.270 --> 10:58.420
I will! I will be your wife!

10:58.420 --> 11:02.720
There is no greater honor for a lupine 
woman than to have a strong husband!

11:02.720 --> 11:07.220
I can't believe I get to be the 
wife of a man as strong as you!

11:07.220 --> 11:09.990
Uh, no, we're just <i>pretending</i>
to be married...

11:09.990 --> 11:14.640
It matters not what it is, 
Master—I mean, Darling!

11:14.640 --> 11:16.230
D-Darling?!

11:16.830 --> 11:19.640
Now, let us go, Darling!

11:32.200 --> 11:37.500
What an interesting thing you 
humans use to hold information.

11:37.500 --> 11:39.720
I wear one, too. See?

11:40.280 --> 11:42.810
So I'll match you, Darling?

11:42.810 --> 11:44.780
Huh? Well, yeah...

11:46.300 --> 11:47.560
What is it?

11:48.360 --> 11:51.570
My race performs a marriage ritual

11:51.570 --> 11:56.030
in which a mated pair swallows some of the 
bones from prey they hunted together,

11:56.030 --> 11:58.180
taking shared possession of it.

11:59.620 --> 12:02.900
The idea of having a matching 
accessory reminded me of that.

12:02.900 --> 12:05.950
<i>She's not gonna tell me 
to swallow bones, is she?</i>

12:06.280 --> 12:08.950
What names will you be registering under?

12:09.360 --> 12:11.910
Listen well, human woman!

12:12.270 --> 12:13.370
My name is Fenry—

12:13.370 --> 12:15.250
She'll register as Rys!

12:18.000 --> 12:20.580
I am so sorry, Darling!

12:20.580 --> 12:23.550
I forgot we were avoiding 
the use of our real names!

12:23.550 --> 12:24.890
Don't worry about it.

12:25.410 --> 12:29.320
I doubt anyone will figure out 
what you are in that form.

12:29.320 --> 12:34.900
I'll need you to live as a human from 
now on, so just get used to it slowly.

12:34.900 --> 12:36.270
Darling...

12:38.850 --> 12:40.280
I have an urgent quest!

12:40.280 --> 12:44.490
A large group of psychobears has 
been spotted north of here!

12:44.490 --> 12:47.070
They're headed toward the city right now!

12:47.970 --> 12:52.160
Not the ones that the rumors say 
destroyed the hero's army...

12:52.160 --> 12:56.120
There is no rank requirement! 
Adventurers of any rank are eligible!

12:56.580 --> 13:01.340
This time only, the reward per bear 
slain will be multiplied by ten!

13:02.140 --> 13:06.130
That sounds pretty profitable, 
but we probably shouldn't.

13:06.130 --> 13:07.760
What are you saying?

13:07.760 --> 13:11.590
You could take out an army of 
psychobears in no time, Darling!

13:11.590 --> 13:13.930
No way. Even the hero couldn't handle them.

13:14.200 --> 13:15.950
I definitely can't do it.

13:16.590 --> 13:19.840
In that case, I'll go kill them myself.

13:19.840 --> 13:20.270
Huh?

13:20.700 --> 13:26.480
If I win, it'll prove how strong you 
are, as the one who defeated me!

13:30.050 --> 13:32.970
The forest where the psychobears 
are is around here, right?

13:32.970 --> 13:34.370
It should be...

13:34.370 --> 13:36.710
Oh, there's a house over there.

13:36.710 --> 13:39.710
That must be the vacant house 
the guild said we can use.

13:40.250 --> 13:42.760
Let's use it as a base to 
hunt the psychobears from.

13:42.760 --> 13:43.790
Okay!

13:43.790 --> 13:48.720
But, Darling, I can easily handle 
a few psychobears on my own.

13:48.720 --> 13:51.410
I can't let you do this alone.

13:51.410 --> 13:53.350
I have spells I want to test out, anyway.

13:53.350 --> 13:57.680
As long as we're together, I bet 
we could even defeat the Dark One!

13:57.680 --> 14:02.230
Let's get those psychobears taken 
care of and claim that reward!

14:04.280 --> 14:05.050
Over there!

14:08.240 --> 14:09.950
Psychobears!

14:10.370 --> 14:11.390
So those are...

14:12.810 --> 14:14.540
Hey, those people are knights.

14:14.540 --> 14:16.160
How pathetic.

14:16.160 --> 14:18.500
Let's just ignore those weaklings.

14:18.860 --> 14:22.090
You can't fight with those injuries! 
Stand down, Blossom!

14:34.470 --> 14:35.980
Lightning Bolt!

14:41.630 --> 14:42.720
Wh-What?!

14:42.720 --> 14:44.690
What in the world is going on?

14:49.610 --> 14:50.760
Belano!

14:59.870 --> 15:03.460
Honestly... You're too nice, Darling.

15:03.460 --> 15:05.630
C'mon, don't say that.

15:05.630 --> 15:08.170
Y-You are... Sir Flio!

15:09.700 --> 15:11.670
Looks like you've saved us again.

15:11.670 --> 15:13.640
Thank you so much!

15:13.640 --> 15:15.920
I thought we were done for.

15:15.920 --> 15:18.180
I'm grateful, as well.

15:18.180 --> 15:19.940
I'm glad you're all okay.

15:20.350 --> 15:23.690
We were worried about what 
might have happened to you.

15:23.690 --> 15:26.480
Though we did suspect that 
you would easily survive,

15:26.480 --> 15:29.190
even against a monster like that.

15:29.190 --> 15:30.970
M-Mon—

15:30.970 --> 15:32.640
Who is this lady?

15:32.640 --> 15:34.370
Oh, uh...

15:34.880 --> 15:37.700
<i>We don't want them finding 
out what she really is.</i>

15:38.000 --> 15:41.210
This is Rys, my travel companion.

15:42.340 --> 15:47.000
<i>Darling, why won't you 
introduce me as your wife?</i>

15:47.000 --> 15:50.470
Anyway, what were all of you doing here?

15:55.080 --> 15:56.550
Rys! Look out!

16:07.110 --> 16:08.560
Wh-What the...

16:08.560 --> 16:10.900
I don't know what just happened, either.

16:13.810 --> 16:17.430
You think it realized that 
it could never beat you?

16:17.430 --> 16:19.330
Does that mean you surrendered?

16:22.020 --> 16:23.740
That's rather honorable, in a way.

16:23.740 --> 16:26.880
Still, we can't just let it go.

16:30.400 --> 16:35.260
Why don't we take this psychobear 
as our subordina—

16:34.040 --> 16:36.640
Um, I think you mean "pet"!

16:36.640 --> 16:39.100
P-P-P-Pet?!

16:39.100 --> 16:43.400
Psychobears are ferocious pests 
that even bested the hero's army.

16:43.400 --> 16:46.950
If we command one, it will look great 
on our list of accomplishments!

16:46.950 --> 16:49.110
I don't care about that, but...

16:49.110 --> 16:51.740
Preventing it from attacking 
people again is a good idea.

16:52.810 --> 16:53.950
Restriction!

16:57.840 --> 17:01.870
This should stop it from 
suddenly going all wild again,

17:01.870 --> 17:04.400
but we can't just walk 
around with it like this.

17:04.400 --> 17:05.330
I know!

17:05.660 --> 17:07.170
Shapeshift!

17:13.460 --> 17:15.290
Now we can walk around with it.

17:16.680 --> 17:18.490
What is this feeling?

17:18.490 --> 17:21.850
It's not nearly as impressive, 
but it's still...

17:21.850 --> 17:23.440
What shall we name it?

17:23.440 --> 17:25.100
Well, it's a psychobear, so...

17:25.430 --> 17:27.240
How about Sybe?

17:26.000 --> 17:28.060
<i>Just what are these people?</i>

17:27.240 --> 17:29.220
That's a fine name!

17:28.060 --> 17:31.470
<i>Not only did they defeat all 
those psychobears in one blow,</i>

17:31.470 --> 17:33.320
<i>but now they're taming one?</i>

17:34.700 --> 17:35.820
Sir Flio...

17:36.300 --> 17:38.900
I wish to ask you a favor.

17:41.020 --> 17:44.950
You've saved us from danger 
twice now. Thank you.

17:45.300 --> 17:47.670
We'd like to formally introduce ourselves.

17:48.000 --> 17:52.380
I am Balirossa, a knight of Klyrode.

17:52.780 --> 17:54.560
I'm Blossom.

17:54.560 --> 17:58.720
I use the strength I got working on my 
family's farm to serve as a Heavy Fighter.

17:58.720 --> 18:01.870
My name is Byleri.

18:01.870 --> 18:04.970
I used to take care of the army's horses,

18:04.970 --> 18:08.440
but at some point, I ended 
up becoming a knight.

18:09.460 --> 18:11.710
Belano. Witch.

18:12.160 --> 18:14.150
I specialize in defensive magic.

18:14.150 --> 18:19.320
Sir Flio, I realize this is a most 
presumptuous thing to ask of you,

18:19.320 --> 18:22.660
but would you please teach
us how to fight?

18:22.660 --> 18:25.220
You want me to train you?

18:26.360 --> 18:28.070
As you know,

18:28.070 --> 18:33.750
the force led by the hero was 
wiped out by psychobears.

18:34.850 --> 18:37.410
The hero was absolutely furious.

18:37.410 --> 18:40.500
He said he wouldn't lead a force against 
the Dark One again until he found

18:40.500 --> 18:42.720
people he could trust to 
serve as his right hand,

18:42.720 --> 18:45.390
and locked himself within the stronghold.

18:46.550 --> 18:50.490
So the king then gave us 
knights an urgent order

18:50.490 --> 18:55.270
to dedicate ourselves to combat until we 
can kill beasts on the psychobears' level.

18:56.760 --> 18:58.310
As embarrassing as it is to say,

18:58.310 --> 19:01.460
we are still relatively new to the order.

19:01.460 --> 19:05.460
The four of us together still aren't 
enough to kill one psychobear.

19:05.460 --> 19:07.860
Please help us.

19:08.420 --> 19:10.500
I don't know...

19:10.930 --> 19:15.460
<i>I'm not even sure exactly 
how magic works myself.</i>

19:15.460 --> 19:17.500
<i>I can't teach anyone.</i>

19:20.840 --> 19:24.220
What shameless women you are!

19:24.940 --> 19:28.890
Um, I introduced her as my 
travel companion before,

19:28.890 --> 19:31.490
but this is actually my wife.

19:31.490 --> 19:34.530
And all I'd really like to do 
is live a quiet life with her.

19:37.060 --> 19:39.340
Huh? Y-Your wife?!

19:39.340 --> 19:42.010
Sir Flio, you're married?

19:42.010 --> 19:46.090
I-I see. We wouldn't want 
to get in your way, then.

19:46.090 --> 19:47.680
That's a shame.

19:49.800 --> 19:52.840
I think it's a good idea, Darling!

19:52.840 --> 19:55.320
You should show them how to fight
by actually fighting them!

19:55.320 --> 19:56.750
Huh? Rys?!

20:00.690 --> 20:04.620
As your wife, I know better than anyone

20:04.620 --> 20:09.970
that you're a kind man who 
can't abandon those in need!

20:09.970 --> 20:14.580
And as your wife, naturally, 
I will abide by your decision!

20:14.580 --> 20:16.810
Yes, as your <i>wife</i>!

20:17.520 --> 20:23.220
<i>I'm not such a good guy that I can give 
more than what I have out of charity.</i>

20:23.220 --> 20:24.410
<i>But...</i>

20:31.260 --> 20:34.330
I'm not too confident that 
I can teach you well,

20:34.850 --> 20:36.930
but if that's all right with you...

20:38.830 --> 20:40.910
We are most grateful, Sir Flio!

20:40.910 --> 20:42.790
Can you start right away?

20:42.790 --> 20:44.930
I'd like to start now, as well!

20:46.510 --> 20:50.350
As long as we're asking too much, 
we have one other request.

20:50.790 --> 20:53.980
It's dangerous to camp out in this area.

20:54.420 --> 20:56.710
Can we rent some of your space?

20:56.710 --> 20:58.970
Just a corner of the living room is enough.

20:58.970 --> 21:00.610
We won't get in your way.

21:00.610 --> 21:01.610
Huh?

21:01.610 --> 21:03.440
I think that would be fine!

21:03.440 --> 21:04.930
We have enough rooms.

21:04.930 --> 21:07.940
You and I can always share a bed, anyway!

21:07.940 --> 21:08.540
What?!

21:08.540 --> 21:12.200
That's only natural since 
we're married, Darling!

21:13.690 --> 21:16.510
What?!

21:25.530 --> 21:28.720
Dark One, I bring a report for <i>mew</i>.

21:28.720 --> 21:31.640
Ah, Uliminas. What is it?

21:32.080 --> 21:34.430
Regarding the annihilated 
unit led by Fengaryl

21:34.430 --> 21:37.530
that was stationed in the Delaveza Forest...

21:37.530 --> 21:41.980
The Purification spell was not cast 
by mages of the Kingdom of Klyrode.

21:42.460 --> 21:45.570
We <i>nyow</i> know that it was 
cast by an individual.

21:47.570 --> 21:50.870
What will <i>mew</i> do, Dark One?

21:51.830 --> 21:58.660
An individual with magic powerful 
enough to instantly eliminate demons?

22:00.280 --> 22:05.470
Find this individual and 
capture them at any cost.

23:40.780 --> 23:42.380
Now that we're a mated pair,

23:42.380 --> 23:45.020
let's wear matching outfits 
and pajamas, Darling!

23:45.020 --> 23:46.570
Huh? That's not a rule, though...

23:47.470 --> 23:49.980
Sybe agrees that matching 
looks would be best!

23:49.980 --> 23:51.400
You understand what he's saying?

23:53.950 --> 23:56.960
You can do next episode 
previews, too! How wonderful!

23:56.960 --> 23:58.330
Uh, he didn't, though.

23:57.620 --> 24:00.000
<b>Next Time</b>

23:57.620 --> 24:00.000
<b>I've Begun My Life in Another World</b>

23:58.330 --> 23:59.570
Please do it right.
